diff --git a/README b/README
index acf2bb7..3babd6a 100644
--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -22,9 +22,18 @@ First, you must install these libraries:
 
 	a. OpenGL (-lGL)
 	b. SDL (-lSDL)
-	c. TCL (-ltcl8.6)
+	c. TCL 8.6 or newer (discovered with pkg-config)
 	d. ALSA (-lasound)
 
+The build also needs pkg-config, Autoconf, Automake and a C++ compiler.
+SDL 1.2 headers/libraries are required; sdl12-compat can provide them.
+SDL 2, SDL 3 and sdl2-compat alone are not sufficient.
+
+On Fedora, install the build dependencies with:
+
+	sudo dnf install gcc-c++ make autoconf automake pkgconf-pkg-config \
+	  SDL-devel mesa-libGL-devel tcl-devel alsa-lib-devel
+
 To build for the first time type these commands in a shell,
 
 a. autoreconf -fvi
@@ -44,6 +53,37 @@ b. rm -rf ~/.din
 
 Now follow the steps for building DIN Is Noise for the first time.
 
+Diagnosing crashes on Fedora:
+
+Keep a backup of ~/.din rather than deleting your saved work. To build
+with checked C++ containers, sanitizers and usable debugger symbols:
+
+	autoreconf -fvi
+	./configure CXXFLAGS="-Og -g3 -D__LINUX_ALSA__ -D_GLIBCXX_DEBUG -fno-fast-math -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer" \
+	  CFLAGS="-Og -g3 -fsanitize=address,undefined" \
+	  LDFLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined"
+	make clean
+	make
+	sudo make install
+
+Normal builds no longer strip debugger symbols automatically.
+Use make install-strip only when stripped binaries are desired.
+DIN needs its installed factory data to initialise ~/.din on first launch.
+If audio cannot be initialised, startup reports an error rather than
+continuing with unallocated audio buffers. Audio preferences must specify
+two output channels and positive sample rates and buffer sizes.
+
+The standalone curve regression tests need no SDL, Tcl or audio device:
+
+	make -C tests CXX=g++ check
+	make -C tests CXX=g++ check-tcl
+	make -C tests clean
+
+These cover clearing/rebuilding curves, endpoint tangent edits,
+Catmull-Rom conversion, vertex removal and empty/nonempty profiles.
+The optional check-tcl target requires Tcl development files and verifies
+command argument handling and ownership of interpreter results.
+
